Yesterday I successfully installed 5.0-RC1 on a four-processor
AS4100.  Overnight I tried a `make -j 8 -s buildworld', but it wasn't
even remotely close to completing after nine hours (probably due to
contention for giant, if what I saw in `top' is any indication).  I
restarted the build without `-j' and things seem to be getting pretty
close to completion.  Congratulations are due to everybody involved in
making this weird hardware behave reliably....

